course: dictionary
lesson: 12678
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around them, tells you which meaning the writer means. «The distressed kitten mewed under the hedge.» A kitten cannot be angry or confused in that way, and it is hurt or frightened, so distressed means very upset or in pain.
explain: «Her distressed jeans had rips at the knees.» Jeans cannot feel upset, and the rips show that someone made them look worn on purpose. Ask yourself: does this meaning fit the sentence? If it does not, try another meaning.
explain: Look for clue words. Sadness, rescue and danger point to one meaning. Rips, scratches and old-looking wood point to another. Money trouble in a business is a third meaning, so always check the clues before you choose.
fact: Distressed means very upset, worried or in pain.
fact: A distressed swimmer is in danger and needs help.
fact: Distressed furniture or jeans are made to look old and worn on purpose, with scratches or rips.
fact: In business, a distressed company is in money trouble.
fact: Useful phrases: «deeply distressed», «distressed by», «distressed jeans», «distressed wood».
exercise: «Her distressed jeans had rips at the knees.» What does distressed mean here? | Lost in the woods | Clean and brand new | *Made to look old and worn on purpose | Very upset and in pain
exercise: «The distressed sailors waved a flag for help.» What does distressed suggest? | In money trouble only | Made to look old and worn | Very happy and calm | *In danger and needing help
exercise: «The puppy was distressed and shivering in the rain.» What does distressed mean? | Full of money | *Very upset, worried or in pain | Made to look old on purpose | Very tidy and clean
test: «The company was distressed and could not pay its workers.» What does distressed mean in this sentence? | *In money trouble | Very upset and worried | In danger at sea | Made to look old on purpose
test: «She was distressed by the news and cried all afternoon.» What does distressed mean here? | *Very upset | Made to look old and worn | Rich and proud | In danger and needing rescue
exam: Which meaning of distressed fits best in «a distressed wood table»? | *Made to look old and worn on purpose | In danger at sea | In money trouble | Very upset
